    {
      "id": "tXFvGLBf-S4zSuyaVcIgZ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 229.080299086737,
      "y": 1207.419700913263,
      "width": 824,
      "height": 750,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aC",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1006808342,
      "version": 1323,
      "versionNonce": 671931210,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785657337928,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1.Setter injection is a Depedency injection  that allows us to\ninject dependency through segtter methods .\n\n2. A developer updates the dependency manually after object \ncreation .\n\n3. As a result object recieves appropriate dependencies when\nsetter methods are called .\n\n---->>>>> $2DIEx-2\n\n\n** Setter always replaces the constructor..\n\n\n\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n                      Field Injection\n                      =============\n\nclass Student{                           class UseStudent{\n    private vehilce v;                          psvm(){\n  ......                                              Bus bus=new Bus();\n                                                    Student s=new Student();\n}                                                   s.v=bus;\n                                                   .....      \n                                                    }\n                                                 }",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1.Setter injection is a Depedency injection  that allows us to\ninject dependency through segtter methods .\n\n2. A developer updates the dependency manually after object \ncreation .\n\n3. As a result object recieves appropriate dependencies when\nsetter methods are called .\n\n---->>>>> $2DIEx-2\n\n\n** Setter always replaces the constructor..\n\n\n\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n                      Field Injection\n                      =============\n\nclass Student{                           class UseStudent{\n    private vehilce v;                          psvm(){\n  ......                                              Bus bus=new Bus();\n                                                    Student s=new Student();\n}                                                   s.v=bus;\n                                                   .....      \n                                                    }\n                                                 }",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "b5tVdEW9HmT0YqL76CTSW",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 224.57347030745584,
      "y": 2001.9379063928416,
      "width": 661,
      "height": 200,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aD",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 958385302,
      "version": 370,
      "versionNonce": 412791702,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785657470657,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "There is a technique in java to access private members outside the\nclass called as Reflection.\n\nThis voilets the very important concept of oops that is \nencapsulation.\n\nthus from spring 4 onwards it is not recommended to use\nfield injection .",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "There is a technique in java to access private members outside the\nclass called as Reflection.\n\nThis voilets the very important concept of oops that is \nencapsulation.\n\nthus from spring 4 onwards it is not recommended to use\nfield injection .",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
