      "seed": 1088966218,
      "version": 1398,
      "versionNonce": 1589662166,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785658858264,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n             Now : DI through Spring\n                     ================\n\n    How Spring Helps in DI?\n    -----------------------------\n\n1.  Till now we implemented DI through java code .\n\n2. However spring framework can also perform  DI automatically .\nthats probably the biggest reason to use Spring for projects.\n\nQuestion : Why we want spring to create object and manage dependecies\nif programmer can do it using new keyword ?\n\nAnswer -> Its not a problem to manage dependecies and creating object \nourself, but wouldn't it be nice to manage dependencies in better way.\n\nImagine project having 100s of classes.\n\nManaging large number of objects may be very difficult thus spring comes \nthere for rescue this problem.\n\nInstead of constructing dependecies , object can retrieve dependencies\nfrom spring .\n\nAll we need to do is to provide container with appropriate configuration.\n\nSpring manages DI using special software called IOC container . \n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n             Now : DI through Spring\n                     ================\n\n    How Spring Helps in DI?\n    -----------------------------\n\n1.  Till now we implemented DI through java code .\n\n2. However spring framework can also perform  DI automatically .\nthats probably the biggest reason to use Spring for projects.\n\nQuestion : Why we want spring to create object and manage dependecies\nif programmer can do it using new keyword ?\n\nAnswer -> Its not a problem to manage dependecies and creating object \nourself, but wouldn't it be nice to manage dependencies in better way.\n\nImagine project having 100s of classes.\n\nManaging large number of objects may be very difficult thus spring comes \nthere for rescue this problem.\n\nInstead of constructing dependecies , object can retrieve dependencies\nfrom spring .\n\nAll we need to do is to provide container with appropriate configuration.\n\nSpring manages DI using special software called IOC container . \n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
